  "description": "#5140 Phase 3a — `duplicate_block` copies a content block and its content subtree as ROWS, right after the original. A fenced block stays ONE block whether or not its fence is closed (the markdown round-trip it replaced split on every newline), the open-fence block's child travels with it while the page nested in the same subtree does not, and the copy carries the ref-typed property with its target, the task columns, the list style and the recurrence rule (#5160 P4), not an occurrence's `repeat-seq`. The returns pin every created row, root first then its descendants in pre-order, with the root one slot after the original. Seed: S1 (Home) > S2 (closed fence), S3 (open fence) > [S4 (child), S5 (nested page) > S6], S7 (carries a ref to S9), S8 (DONE task), S9 (ref target) > S11 (purged by an op), S10 (trashed by an op). Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
